  "full_text": "Sometimes I think of time travel and like there's the future and there's the past. And we're told, you know, I say I love God. And for me, coming from an evolution point, I like the God of the Bible. But maybe that's not God. Maybe that's Satan's work. Maybe you shouldn't love evolution. Maybe it's Satan. I don't know. Is it possible to make a case for that? See, I assumed that the world was created by God, but technically Satan had a part in it. So if you love God, maybe it's not quite the same as loving creation. So anyway, what if there's Satan's work in... Creation or something. I don't know just we're kind of returning to more Orthodox Catholicism It's good to do that so that it's possible for the next generation to be saved because I started from Catholicism and If you can't return it back to Catholicism, it's kind of a messed up situation so",
